Package: sekashot
Version: @VERSION@
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: KrisDewa <krisdewa@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/krisdewa/Sekashot
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-pyqt6
Recommends: grim, wl-clipboard, xclip, python3-pyqt6.qtmultimedia, python3-xlib, python3-pynput, python3-dbus, libnotify-bin
Suggests: gtk-update-icon-cache
Description: Screenshot tool with annotations
 Sekashot captures the screen on Print Screen, freezes the desktop behind a
 dimmed overlay and lets you drag out a selection with a live pixel-size
 readout.
 .
 Annotate the selection with pen, line, arrow, rectangle, marker, text and
 blur, then copy or save it. Notifications report where a capture landed, so
 an auto-saved file is never lost in a folder nobody was looking at.
 .
 On Wayland the hotkey comes from the compositor (see
 'sekashot --install-hotkey'); on X11 the application grabs the key itself.
